+-   **Performance:** Rendering performance is comparable to converting the buffer to a normal mesh, as the vertex shader runs for each vertex in the buffer but generates no fragments for unused ones [S2, unofficial]. For complex scenes, an append buffer or counter buffer might be more efficient to avoid processing zero-area triangles [S2, unofficial].
 -   **Strengths:** Massive parallelism, no dynamic allocation during extraction, simple rendering pipeline integration via `DrawProcedural` [S2, unofficial].
 -   **Limitations:** Fixed-size buffer leads to memory waste if the surface area is small. Boundary handling requires explicit checks or padding [S2, unofficial]. When `delta` (v2 - v1) is 0.0f, the offset is set to 0.5f to avoid division by zero, handling flat regions where the surface is parallel to the edge [S2, unofficial].
